meta {
  name: gupshup-plutus
}

docs {
  # plutus-api Gupshup endpoints

  The plutus-api side of Gupshup: the VAHN_ADMIN test endpoints that call Gupshup through
  `GupshupSmsClient` / `GupshupWhatsappClient`, and the inbound webhook. For direct calls to
  Gupshup itself, see the `gupshup` folder.

  ## Test endpoints (`/api/gupshup/test/*`)

  - `@RolesAllowed(VAHN_ADMIN)`: `{{accessToken}}` must belong to a VAHN_ADMIN user. Log in
    with "Send OTP" / "Verify OTP" using an admin phone first; a driver token gets 403.
  - These send a **real** SMS or WhatsApp message. The recipient is read from
    `GUPSHUP_TEST_PHONE` in `bruno/collections/plutus-api/.env` (gitignored), a 10-digit number
    or one with the `91` prefix.
  - Response is `200 {"success":true,"message":"...","provider":"GUPSHUP"}`, or `500` with
    `success:false` when Gupshup rejects the request. Details are only in the plutus logs.

  ## Webhook (`/webhooks/gupshup`)

  Unauthenticated and always returns `200`. It logs the body when
  `gupshup.webhook.logging_enabled` is on and relays the raw bytes to crm-service.
}
